# Sidequest: Raise a Chocobo ({1}{G}, enchantment): "When this enchantment enters, create a 2/2 green Bird creature token with
# 'Whenever a land you control enters, this token gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' At the beginning of your first main phase, if you
# control four or more Birds, transform this enchantment." Back: Black Chocobo, a 2/2 Bird creature: "When this permanent
# transforms into Black Chocobo, search your library for a land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.
# Landfall - Whenever a land you control enters, Birds you control get +1/+0 until end of turn."
# On turn 1 Bot1 makes four Birds - the token, Birds of Paradise (1/1), Aven Skirmisher (1/1) and Aven Envoy (1/1) - and the
# trigger is not on the stack yet (it is not a first main phase's beginning). On turn 3 it triggers with exactly four Birds, the
# enchantment becomes the 2/2 creature Black Chocobo, and Bot1 searches: a Lightning Bolt (not a land) is refused, the Mountain
# comes in tapped. That land entering is a landfall for the token (+1/+0) and for Black Chocobo (+1/+0 to every Bird): the token
# is 4/2 (2 +1 +1), Black Chocobo 3/2, and the three 1/1 Birds 2/1. On turn 4 the effects have ended (CR 514.2).

